implementationPlan.description:
Replace the unbounded saga rollback goroutine at engine.go:622-626. Change from:
```go
go func(wfID string) {
    if err := e.saga.Rollback(e.ctx, wfID); err != nil {
        logging.Error("scheduler", "saga rollback failed", ...)
    }
}(workflowID)
```
To:
```go
go func(wfID string) {
    ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 30*time.Second)
    defer cancel()
    start := time.Now()
    if err := e.saga.Rollback(ctx, wfID); err != nil {
        logging.Error("scheduler", "saga rollback failed", "workflow_id", wfID, "duration", time.Since(start), "error", err)
    } else {
        logging.Info("scheduler", "saga rollback completed", "workflow_id", wfID, "duration", time.Since(start))
    }
}(workflowID)
```
Uses `context.Background()` instead of `e.ctx` because rollback must complete even if the engine is shutting down. The 30s timeout bounds the goroutine lifetime.
